<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Glaphyra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Glaphyra was a Cappadocian princess, daughter of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archelaus-of-cappadocia">Archelaus of Cappadocia</a>. She married Alexander, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> executed in 7 BCE, then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-ii">Juba II of Mauretania</a>, and finally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-archelaus">Herod Archelaus</a>, ethnarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judaea</a> and her first husband's half-brother. This last marriage offended Jewish law and added to Archelaus's unpopularity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/glaphyra.jpg" alt="Glaphyra" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Reverdy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glaphyra_medal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
